        "language": "english",
        "review": "I don't like having to say this but I really don't like this game. They streamlined Eden's gameplay to such an extent where it barely feels the same. The swinging is just this automatic thing you start doing at full speed, in the first game swinging is all physics based to where you actually have to start yourself going to get speed to jump up via letting go. This game feels wrong and scratches against my brain in an odd way because of the unnecessary change to the raw gameplay. I'll keep playing this to see if it grows on me but if you're like me who played the original game in 2009 and it's such a soft spot for you with it's unique gameplay, it's a completely different thing here and you might like it more but I definitely like it less.",
